{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1559599-new-htv-player-starting-character-effectiveness-questions","id":1559599,"title":"New HtV player - starting character effectiveness questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-04-24T06:36:57-07:00","id":1559599,"title":"New HtV player - starting character effectiveness questions","content":"I'm thinking of joining an online game of HtV having only ever played Mage. In Mage I know roughly what makes a useful starting character but mortal Hunters feel much harder. 2e removes some of the temptation to min max on character creation but there are lots of places where it looks like you could create a character who is too one dimensional or too spread out because you don't have anything close to the obvious built in usefulness of arcana.<br /> <br /> Can a character be useful with low to middling combat skills (dex 2 and firearms 2 for instance) or should a character with those skills be thought of an a non-combatant? Similarly, how important is taking backup physical skills like brawl or weapon 1 on a character who wants to avoid close combat as much as possible?<br /> <br /> What skill covers reloading ammo and would it be expected that a character could do that in game (skill + time + perhaps a resource dot to get the silver) to create silver bullets or would it be something that needs a merit dot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28478-madmarcus","name":"Madmarcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-25T12:13:16-07:00","id":1559621,"title":"","content":"Hurtlocker is going to be your friend man. Using other Skills Voilent, Rules for Reloads, and many other fun stuff to look though. <br /> <br /> Generally Hunter is an Investigation game, both of the social and mental kind, so being more focuse on one of those feilds isnt a bad thing. <br /> Having some back updots for Attacks isnt a bad thing, could just do a team work action in combat to hopefully give an attacker damage. <br /> Hopefully you can talk with your other Cell mates to see what htey need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-25T13:38:31-07:00","id":1559623,"title":"","content":"I think you're making a lot of assumptions about the game that are really down to the particular style of the ST. CofD games don't generally assume that combat is a necessary element, but equally, it's perfectly possible for a game to be quite combat-heavy. It's down to the way the ST runs the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can a character be useful with low to middling combat skills (dex 2 and firearms 2 for instance) or should a character with those skills be thought of an a non-combatant? </div> </div> </div>Given a firearm, they can probably be somewhat relied upon.<br /> <br /> Then again, who or what are you fighting? If, for example, Dracula needs to be staked through the heart and doesn't care about bullets, then your firearm skills suddenly become less useful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly, how important is taking backup physical skills like brawl or weapon 1 on a character who wants to avoid close combat as much as possible? </div> </div> </div>Brawl is helpful in tough spots where you aren't able to come armed or have been disarmed... But whether that occurs or not is kinda down to the ST. Banes and items that do serious damage to monsters (such as the aforementioned stake through the heart) are usually weapons, though that's more a narrative convention than a hard rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What skill covers reloading ammo and would it be expected that a character could do that in game (skill + time + perhaps a resource dot to get the silver) to create silver bullets or would it be something that needs a merit dot? </div> </div> </div>Crafts probably. Maybe take a specialty in reloading ammunition to avoid any doubt.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-25T19:07:41-07:00","id":1559629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cross-a-way</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1559599-new-htv-player-starting-character-effectiveness-questions?p=1559621#post1559621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully you can talk with your other Cell mates to see what they need.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the rub. This is an online game with many players. Player sheets are private and character creation is not done in connection with other players. It is assumed that your character will find their niche after creation. I like it as a break from ttrpg groups planning all the character so that they fit neatly together but it does bump up the anxiety about making a marginally useful character.<br /> <br /> Similarly, because it is a big game with multiple scenes ongoing at the same time there is little reason to assume any specific type of threat is more likely. The only thing defined is that the clashes between hunters are ramped up an some conspiracies are definitely on the antagonist side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28478-madmarcus","name":"Madmarcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}